[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=GNOME Keyring Environment Sync
Comment=Imports GNOME_KEYRING_CONTROL/SSH_AUTH_SOCK from the PAM-unlocked login keyring into the systemd --user manager, so D-Bus-activated services (e.g. org.freedesktop.secrets) reuse the already-unlocked keyring instead of spawning a second, locked daemon that repeatedly prompts for a password.
Exec=systemctl --user import-environment GNOME_KEYRING_CONTROL SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Terminal=false
StartupNotify=false
